Q: How to conditionally show/hide and make fields required in nested Drupal paragraphs based on parent block field selection? A: <p>have a look at states, I saw an example and I think this might help</p>
<pre><code>// In your custom module file (e.g., mymodule.module) or custom form class

$form['testfield'] = array(
  '#type' =&gt; 'select',
  '#title' =&gt; t('Select an option'),
  '#options' =&gt; array(
    'a' =&gt; 'Option A',
    'b' =&gt; 'Option B',
    'c' =&gt; 'Option C',
  ),
);

$form['display_field'] = array(
  '#title' =&gt; t('This field displays for Option B'),
  '#type' =&gt; 'textfield',
  // Define the conditional logic here
  '#states' =&gt; array(
    // Action to take: 'visible' or 'invisible', 'enabled' or 'disabled', etc.
    'visible' =&gt; array(
      // The selector for the controlling input element
      ':input[name=&quot;testfield&quot;]' =&gt; array(
        // Condition and value
        'value' =&gt; 'b',
      ),
    ),
  ),
);
</code></pre>

Q: How to round decimal of double in java A: <p>You can search for your number by assigning a tolerance margin for the result, something like:</p>
<pre><code>double tolerance = 0.000005, 
       objetive = 0.000235, 
       min = objetive - tolerance,
       max = objetive + tolerance,
       list[] = { 0.0001, 0.00023, 0.00024 }; 

for( int i = 0; i &lt; list.length; i++ ) {
   if( min &lt; list[ i ] &amp;&amp; max &gt; list[ i ] ) {
      System.out.println( &quot;Eureka&quot; );
      System.out.println( i );
      break;
   }
}
</code></pre>
